{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"REVIEWER FAILURE CENSUS - failures of the four TOOLS under evaluation, harness failures excluded and listed separately. Written up at wave3/REVIEWER_FAILURES.md. THE DENOMINATOR PROBLEM FIRST: a census of surviving artifacts systematically under-reports tool failure, because a failed run was re-run and the retry overwrote it. All 20 Wave 3 mini runs read Submitted today, yet java-gradle died at its 150-step budget and only succeeded on a higher-budget retry; the surviving file shows no trace. Rates therefore come from per-call telemetry first, the preserved failure archive second, and the narrative record last - where only the narrative exists a count is a floor, not a rate. REBAR: 12 of 385 LLM calls failed (3.1 percent) across 3 of 11 runs, all recovered by retry, every run producing a verdict; all 12 share finish_reason tool_call on the frontier class, the reviewer terminating on a tool call instead of producing its finding payload, and 10 of the 12 fell in the single run that then scored 22 true positives of 23. Deterministic precheck refused without any content review on 17 of 220 Wave 1 candidates (7.7 percent). Indeterminate findings are 20 percent of PASS output and zero on any BLOCK run. Detected-then-withdrawn accounts for 5 of 241 misses. MINI: the only arm with a total-loss mode - it consumes the whole step budget and submits nothing, and the budget binds on REPOSITORY size rather than plan size, which makes its failure probability a property of the target repo rather than the review task. Separately emits unparseable JSON from unescaped quotes, recoverable by mechanical repair, once per 20 Wave 3 runs. COMPOUND ENGINEERING: loses whole personas with no error surfaced - four occurrences now, and coherence specifically three times. The orchestrator synthesizes from whichever personas returned and produces a normal-looking review; a run that does not volunteer the gap is indistinguishable from a complete one. This biases CE totals DOWNWARD, so leaving it uncorrected would flatter rebar. SUPERPOWERS: silently executes the reviewer in-session when subagent dispatch is unavailable, with no marker in the artifact."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443113777073001,"uuid":"5954450c-70b2-4540-b5b4-603c1c739d65"}